
!data/corpus/.keep
!data/fallback/.keep
# Client drawings never enter the repository. The folder is kept so the
# Dockerfile can copy it; its contents are not ours to publish.
# Recorded fallback runs (scripts/freeze_run.py) hold rendered pages of the
# Transfer tarballs used to move a delta onto this machine. The mount does
# client's drawings and the client's own quantities. Same rule as the corpus:
# generated per host, never committed. The folder is kept so the image build
# has somewhere to copy from when an operator has deliberately frozen one.
# not allow deletes, so they are ignored rather than left to be committed.
*.egg-info/
*.py[cod]
.env
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
Claude outputs/
_*.tar.gz
__pycache__/
cdk.out/
data/corpus/*
data/fallback/*
data/state/
